name: Hook performance profile (advisory)

# Sprint 10 PLAN-010 Phase 2. Advisory, measure-only per ADR-024.
# Converts to a blocking gate in Sprint 11 IFF three consecutive
# weekly runs show p99 stable within 20% variance (ADR-024 §Decision).

on:
  schedule:
    # Monday 06:00 UTC — PLAN-012 §S6 cron stagger. Chaos runs 03:00,
    # perf-profile 06:00, otel-smoke 09:00, adapter-live 12:00. See
    # .github/workflows/_README.md for the full schedule + rationale.
    - cron: '0 6 * * 1'
  workflow_dispatch:
  push:
    branches: [main]
    paths:
      - '.claude/hooks/**'
      - '.claude/scripts/hook-profiler.py'
      - '.github/workflows/perf-profile.yml'

concurrency:
  group: perf-profile-${{ github.ref }}
  cancel-in-progress: true

permissions:
  contents: read

jobs:

### .github/workflows/reality-ledger.yml
# PLAN-071 §4.5 Phase 4 — Reality Ledger advisory CI workflow
#
# Weekly drift-detection run. Advisory-only — never blocks CI; opens or
# updates a SINGLE ongoing GitHub issue when findings exist (idempotent
# per ADR-064 precedent).
#
# Schedule offset 09:00 UTC = 2h after tier-policy.yml (07:00 UTC) per
# Round 1 R-SEC U6 to avoid runner contention.
#
# Security envelope (9 explicit checks per §4.5):
#   1. Trigger: ONLY workflow_dispatch + schedule (no PR triggers)
#   2. Permissions: contents:read + issues:write (deny-by-default)
#   3. Fork-PR guard at job level
#   4. Checkout SHA-pinned + persist-credentials:false
#   5. timeout-minutes: 15 job cap
#   6. Concurrency group with cancel-in-progress:false
#   7. ALL uses: SHA-pinned (validate-governance.sh enforces)
#   8. Zero secrets.* except GITHUB_TOKEN
#   9. Concurrency block declared (R2 G1)

name: reality-ledger

on:
  workflow_dispatch:
  schedule:
    - cron: "0 9 * * 1"  # Monday 09:00 UTC

permissions:

### .github/workflows/red-team.yml
name: Red-team adversarial eval (State 1 — enforcing)

# PLAN-014 Phase D.3 (ADJ-018). State 1 enforcement:
# - PR path: exit-1 on regression (blocks merge)
# - Schedule path: exit-0 + issue creation (backward compatible)
# - Timeout bumped to 30 min for 80-fixture corpus
# - Fork-PR policy: PRs from forks touching hooks/red-team require
#   re-open from intra-repo branch
#
# Previous: PLAN-013 Phase D.6 advisory (State 0).
# ADR-037 Transition Log: State 0 -> 1 evidence at
# .claude/scripts/red-team-corpus/v1/fixtures.jsonl.sha256
#
# Flake budget (PLAN-013 consensus S17): max 1/week tolerated per
# fixture; 2+ failures in 7-day window auto-quarantine the fixture
# in `.claude/scripts/red-team-corpus/flake-budget.yaml` and open an
# issue requesting root-cause analysis. Quarantined fixtures are
# SKIPPED until RCA sign-off + 7 consecutive clean runs.

on:
  schedule:
    # Monday 15:00 UTC. Non-collision slot -- PLAN-012 uses 03/06/09/12.
    - cron: '0 15 * * 1'
  workflow_dispatch:
  push:
    branches: [main]
    paths:
      - '.claude/scripts/red-team-eval.py'

### .github/workflows/release.yml
name: Release

on:
  push:
    tags:
      - "v*"

concurrency:
  group: release-${{ github.ref }}
  cancel-in-progress: false

jobs:
  release-gate:
    # PLAN-012 Phase 2 CEO_SOTA_DISABLE parity.
    if: vars.CEO_SOTA_DISABLE != '1'
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    # 20 -> 35 (S300, corte da rc.2): o gate da rc.1 levou 18m37s
    # (margem de 1m23s) e o attempt-1 da rc.2 ESTOUROU os 20 min com
    # ~10 min de stalls das suites em runner 2-core carregado (classe
    # ADR-163/perf-under-load) — o passo do verdito imprimiu all-green
    # 13ms antes do machado. Mesma regra anti-flake dos budgets do
    # smoke/nightly: folga primeiro, re-apertar com p95 real acumulado.
    timeout-minutes: 35
    permissions:
      # `contents: read` for checkout; `actions: read` lets the
      # weekly-workflow status gate (see below) call `gh run list`
      # against the public Actions REST API.
      contents: read

### .github/workflows/shadow-ci.yml
name: Shadow CI — Skill Patch Benchmarks (advisory)

# PLAN-012 Phase 3 D4 / ADR-031 §5.
#
# Runs benchmarks against `<SKILL.md>.shadow.md` files and posts a PR
# comment + uploads a report artifact. NEVER auto-merges. Owner merges
# manually after review.
#
# Security contract (debate round 1 Security HIGH-2):
#   - `pull_request` trigger ONLY. NEVER `pull_request_target` — skill
#     patches are executable instructions for future agents (CWE-94),
#     so running PR-author code with write perms is unacceptable
#     (CVE-2020-27151 pattern).
#   - `permissions: contents: read` + `pull-requests: write`. No
#     `contents: write`, no `id-token: write`.
#   - Concurrency: per-ref group; `cancel-in-progress: false` so
#     in-flight shadow runs finish (race exercised by
#     test_shadow_apply_kill.py).
#   - SHA-pinned actions (Sprint 7 convention).
#   - 20-min timeout.
#
# `run-skill-shadow-bench.py` is a Sprint 12 follow-up. Until it ships
# the step emits a stub "runner not yet shipped" report. Workflow
# stays VALID + advisory without the runner.
#
# Kill-switch: `CEO_SOTA_DISABLE=1` short-circuits (PLAN-011 §S4).

on:

### .github/workflows/smoke-install.yml
name: Smoke Install

on:
  pull_request:
    paths:
      - "scripts/install.sh"
      - "scripts/upgrade.sh"
      # PLAN-161 (CI wiring): upgrade oracles + the manifest lib they
      # exercise — keep BOTH filter lists (pull_request + push) in sync.
      - "scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh"
      # The ownership + parity e2e call _hash_file/_hash_stdin from here, and
      # this workflow is their ONLY CI execution — without the helper in the
      # filter, a PR touching only it skips the gate entirely (codex W1
      # round 10, P2: the "red gate nobody runs" class, one level deeper).
      - "scripts/_hash_lib.sh"
      - "scripts/tests/test-upgrade-dryrun-identity.sh"
      - "scripts/tests/test-upgrade-exclusions.sh"
      - "scripts/tests/smoke-install.sh"
      # PLAN-166 F4 (OQ-4): the install/upgrade parity e2e and its classifier.
      # The finding this closes is "a red gate nobody runs" (5th instance) --
      # an unwired test is the same as no test.
      - "scripts/tests/test-install-upgrade-parity-e2e.sh"
      - "scripts/tests/_parity_classify.py"
      # PLAN-166 F3 (ADR-155-AMEND-1): delivery-record ownership e2e —
      # scripts/tests/*.sh runs ONLY in this workflow (same r11/r20 wiring
      # rule as the parity e2e above).
      - "scripts/tests/test-upgrade-spec-ownership.sh"
      # PLAN-168 W1 (AC-1): the PLAN-167 ownership oracles + their truth

### .github/workflows/supply-chain-watch.yml
# PLAN-153 Wave E item 4 — scheduled supply-chain watch (NEW workflow).
#
# Two watch axes, weekly:
#   (a) workflow policy — SHA-pin format across ALL workflows + policy
#       assertions (no pull_request_target, no unguarded fork-reachable
#       secrets) + tag-comment drift vs upstream, via the extended
#       `.claude/scripts/check-action-sha-drift.py --policy --strict`.
#   (b) npm provenance — the latest published `ceo-orchestration` version
#       still carries a SLSA provenance attestation on the npm registry,
#       still corresponds to a tag in THIS repo, and `npm audit
#       signatures` still verifies (honest-limits note inline below).
# On any red: create/update a SINGLE pinned issue (idempotent, searched
# by label — reality-ledger.yml / ADR-064 precedent) and red the run.
#
# Security envelope (mirrors reality-ledger.yml §4.5 precedent):
#   1. Triggers: schedule + workflow_dispatch ONLY. NEVER pull_request /
#      pull_request_target — nothing here is fork-reachable (would also
#      be self-contradictory: axis (a) enforces exactly that policy).
#   2. Permissions: contents:read baseline; issues:write exists SOLELY
#      for the red-path pinned issue. No other write surface.
#   3. All `uses:` SHA-pinned; checkout persist-credentials:false.
#   4. Zero secrets.* except the ambient GITHUB_TOKEN (gh api + issue).
#      npm registry queries are unauthenticated public reads.
#   5. CEO_SOTA_DISABLE honored at job level (_README.md §R8).
#   6. timeout-minutes bounded; concurrency no-cancel (cron precedent).

name: supply-chain-watch


### .github/workflows/tier-policy.yml
# STAGED: .github/workflows/tier-policy.yml (Phase 5 Owner promotion target)
#
# Owner physical shell moves via kernel batch
# /tmp/plan_043_phase_5_promote_canonical.py (see OWNER-LOCAL-ACTIONS.md).
#
# Per Round 1 closures:
# - C-P0-13 schedule at 07:00 UTC (2h buffer post-tournament 04:00 + 75min cap)
# - C-P0-14 Option B (notify-only): derive + create GH issues; Owner
#   applies LOCALLY. CI does NOT auto-commit.
# - C-P1-8 install.sh compatible (both factors kill-switch enforced
#   at job level: CEO_TIER_POLICY_CI=1 + fork-safety assertion)
# - F-OPS-P0-2 issue dedup: by label + agent + direction
name: tier-policy

on:
  workflow_dispatch:
    inputs:
      dry_run:
        description: "Dry-run only (no issue creation)"
        required: false
        default: "true"
        type: choice
        options: ["true", "false"]
  # Monthly, 07:00 UTC first-of-month. 2h buffer after tournament.yml
  # (04:00 + 75min max runtime) per C-P0-13.
  schedule:
    - cron: "0 7 1 * *"


### .github/workflows/tournament.yml
name: Agent-eval tournament (advisory, cost-bounded)

# PLAN-032 Wave B — ADR-063 empirical ADR-052 dispatch validation.
#
# Trigger surface (Round 1 C-P0 + F-OPS closures):
#   - workflow_dispatch: manual run for Owner-initiated validation
#   - schedule: monthly on 1st at 04:00 UTC (avoids collision with
#     red-team.yml Mon 15:00 UTC and adapter-live.yml Mon 12:00 UTC)
#
# Explicitly NOT triggered on PR (cost discipline — each run $40-120).
# pull_request_target EXPLICITLY FORBIDDEN per PLAN-002 §8 finding #18
# (code-injection vector in forked repo's workflow).
#
# Fork-safety (F-OPS2 closure): IS_FORK_PR env gates issue creation so
# fork PRs can never cause write-access attempts without secret scoping.
#
# Budget (F-OPS4 closure): TOURNAMENT_BUDGET_USD wired from repo secret
# with $75 default (Round 1 recalibrated from miscalibrated $10).
#
# Timeout (F-OPS1 closure): 75-minute job ceiling covers 50-fixture run
# at Tier-2 Anthropic rate-limit with headroom for slow upstream.

on:
  workflow_dispatch:
    inputs:
      fixtures_count:
        description: "Fixtures count (ceiling 50)"
        required: false

### .github/workflows/translations-drift.yml
name: Translations drift

# PLAN-004 Phase 9 (advisory commits-ahead monitor) +
# PLAN-013 Phase B.7 (structural parity enforcement over 9 pairs).
#
# Two jobs:
#   - `drift-check` (PLAN-004, advisory, continue-on-error) — commits-ahead
#     heuristic between README pair.
#   - `structural-parity` (PLAN-013, blocking) — runs
#     `check_translations_drift.py` across all pairs declared in
#     `.claude/scripts/translations-pairs.yaml`; validates heading count,
#     code-fence count, line-count delta ≤10%, bidirectional cross-link.
#
# Cron stagger per `.github/workflows/_README.md` table: Monday 18:00 UTC
# (next free slot after PLAN-012 03/06/09/12 + PLAN-013 red-team 15:00).

on:
  pull_request:
    paths:
      - "README.md"
      - "README.pt-BR.md"
      - "PROTOCOL.md"
      - "PROTOCOL.pt-BR.md"
      - ".claude/team.md"
      - "team.en.md"
      - "CONTRIBUTING.md"
      - "CONTRIBUTING.pt-BR.md"
      - "docs/**.md"

