The static guard/template sets are internally correct for rounds 1–24, and all supplied scripts parse. The blocking problem is lifecycle closure: this very review is round 25 in the same manifest namespace, so recording its result makes the 1–24 templates stale (or forces a post-review template rewrite and another round). I also found one genuine ignored-command-status path in the GA evidence producer and an interruption window that leaves a public GA without the npm half of the release.
Completed the read-only review. Syntax and current 1–24 manifests are clean, but the current review round creates a deterministic manifest/template closure failure, with two additional fail-closed gaps.
  ✓ Inspect the ceremony files, manifests, templates, and relevant guard/validator implementation
  ✓ Model fresh-run and interruption/resume state transitions for RC3 and GA
  ✓ Validate commit allowlists, evidence set equality, and remote receipt selection
  ✓ Produce an evidence-cited GO/NO-GO verdict
codex
P0 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-RC3-CUT.sh:90-120`; `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/verdict-fields-v1.3.0-rc.3.TEMPLATE.md:12-114` — This review becomes round 25 in `repass-rc3-cures/`, while both RC3 templates enumerate only rounds 1–24. Leaving `MANIFEST-cures.sha256` unchanged makes G0 derive `FINAL_N=25` and abort on set equality. Adding round-25 artifacts to the manifest lets G0 pass but makes the local/server delta guard reject the template allowlist after commit 2. Regenerating the templates creates another unreviewed ceremony version and another review round, forming a closure loop. Minimal fix: record ceremony-script reviews in a separate, independently pinned commit-1 evidence directory that is outside the RC3 delta manifest; do not append them to the cure-round namespace enumerated by the templates.

P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-ga/run-ga-repass.sh:207` — `tr` runs inside command substitution. Under `set -uo pipefail` without `-e`, its nonzero status is not seen by the outer `git diff ... || exit`. A read failure after partial output can therefore select only a prefix of the scope; if that diff remains over 50 lines, all hashes and Codex controls can approve incomplete evidence. Minimal fix: capture and check the pathspec in a separate command before invoking `git diff`, or build a checked Bash array.

P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-GA-CUT.sh:557-609` — Once `release.yml` succeeds, the GA Release is already public, but drafting occurs only on an observed npm timeout/failure. Ctrl-C, terminal loss, or host failure during the approval wait leaves a public GA without confirmed npm publication indefinitely; monitor-mode resume does not immediately hide it. Minimal fix: create stable releases as drafts and undraft only after `npm view` and the pinned Publish-step receipt succeed. An EXIT trap is useful for ordinary interruption but does not close power-loss/SIGKILL.

The current round cannot close its own evidence set, and the remaining failure paths are not fail-closed under the ratified threat model.

VERDICT: NO-GO
